== the two call sites the census found
  uuid-shaped n=4  bytes de ad be ef
  version-shaped n=3  14.7.2
== the length modifier decides the width of the store
  %hhu -> 255  guard intact: yes
  %hu  -> 65535  guard intact: yes
  %u   -> 123456  guard intact: yes
  %llu -> 4294967296  (exceeds 32 bits: yes)
== %c does not skip whitespace, everything else does
  leading and inner space skipped: n=2 a=42 b=7
  %c on " x" reads '_' (a space, not 'x'): yes
== bases, signs and widths
  %d(-17)=-17  %x(0x1f)=31  %o(0755)=493  %i(0x2A)=42
  width splits 123456 into n=2 123 and 456
== strings, suppression, %n and %%
  two strings n=2 [alpha] [beta]
  suppression returns only the counted one: n=1
  %n reports consumed=2 (n=1, and %n is not counted)
  %% matches a literal percent: n=1 v=50
== short counts and EOF are different answers
  input shorter than format: n=1 (a=7, b untouched=yes)
  empty input returns EOF: yes
  non-matching input returns 0: yes
done
